WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
The teaching database includes several small datasets.

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:07.712
Patients and admissions support healthcare-style analytical examples.

00:00:07.712 --> 00:00:11.597
Employees includes a manager hierarchy and salary ties.

00:00:11.597 --> 00:00:17.562
Sales supports running totals, moving averages, ranking, and percent-of-total calculations.

00:00:17.562 --> 00:00:20.822
Website visits provides ordered event sequences.

00:00:20.822 --> 00:00:24.462
The variety helps you see that the SQL patterns are general.

00:00:24.462 --> 00:00:29.752
Connect this idea to a sales team calculating running revenue and top products by region.

00:00:29.752 --> 00:00:34.792
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.792 --> 00:00:41.462
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:46.432
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:46.432 --> 00:00:51.760
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
